Back Guide Monitor System Function Outline

The back guide monitor is a system that assists reversing by superimposing distance guide lines, vehicle width extension lines, estimated course lines and parking guide lines on the image from the rear view monitor camera mounted at the rear of the vehicle, and displaying it on the HDD navigation screen. Voice guidance can be output during parallel parking.

When the shift position is moved to "R" (reverse) with the power source mode ON (IG), the display changes to the back guide monitor screen and the image of the area behind the vehicle from the rear view monitor camera is displayed on the HDD navigation screen.

The back guide monitor is an auxiliary device for making it easier to check behind the vehicle; always drive while directly confirming visually that it is safe behind and around the vehicle.
